I think it's a cool idea, but to write a patch -enforcing- this, as
opposed to just making it available as a challenge, you'd have to
implement rules something like the following:

1. If you entered an essential branch, you could not leave it until
obtaining it's goal item.  If it's an optional branch, I'd suggest the
player only have to reach its final level before being allowed to
reverse direction.  (Naturally, for Vlad's Tower, the initial
direction is up, with down becoming available after getting the
Candelabrum.)
2. If you're on a branch and got to its end, I'd suggest you'd be put
on a similarly one-way trip back to the main dungeon.  If you left
mineend without the luckstone or sokoban without its reward, you could
not go back and get it.
3. If you reach a level with a required branch, you'd HAVE to take
it.  If you couldn't take that required branch, you'd have to stay on
that level until you were able.  This is troublesome for the Quest,
obviously, unless the level requirement were relaxed.
4. Out of necessity, essential items would have to be immune to
levelport, falling into holes (at least on the way up), or other
means of changing level in a direction other than the one in which the
player is travelling.
5. You wouldn't be allowed to leave a level without all the essential
items found to that point, unless those items had been moved further
ahead in the dungeon by other means.

